# ntfy collab-loop single-poller coordination lockfile (ADR-0019); runtime-only.
# write_lock's scratch file is named per-writer (`<lock>.<pid>-<rand>.tmp`) so two
# processes writing the lock never share one scratch name; the glob must therefore track
# that shape or a poller killed mid-write strands an untracked file at the project root.
# The `*` also still covers the pre-2026-08-07 fixed `.collab_loop.lock.tmp` name, which
# an older poller copy can still produce across a deploy.
# Guarded by tests/test_collab_loop.py::TestScratchFilesStayUntracked.
#
# Both entries were re-verified on 2026-08-07 with `git check-ignore -q` (exit 0 for
# `.collab_loop.lock`, the legacy `.collab_loop.lock.tmp`, and a live per-writer
# `.collab_loop.lock.<pid>-<rand>.tmp`), so neither is stale. Note what this cannot do:
# ignoring a path only hides a stray artifact from `git status` — it does not stop one being
# created, and the 2026-08-07 incident was a TEST writing a forged-approval payload into the
# LIVE lockfile, which no ignore rule can prevent. That is now stopped upstream by
# `tests/conftest.py` (COLLAB_LOOP_LOCK redirects the path; the write guard refuses the write).
# Deliberately NOT ignored: `probe.lock` and other ad-hoc probe artifacts. A stray in the
# working tree should stay visible — a forgotten one was how the third contamination was found.
.collab_loop.lock
.collab_loop.lock*.tmp

# Session-local worktrees — see spawn_project's EXCLUDE_PATTERNS for the propagation guard
.claude/worktrees/

# Session wrap-up runtime state (ADR-0018): occupancy sidecars + debounce flags,
# and the auto-generated handoff artifacts. Both carry session/model metadata and
# must never be committed.
.claude/hooks/.state/
docs/handoff/

# /goal-loop runtime loop-state (ADR-0026): the atomically-written per-goal tick record
# is mutable runtime data (re-derived + untrusted on read), never a committed artifact.
loops/.state/

# Telemetry A3 (ADR-0020): the real subscription fee is personal financial
# metadata — only config/subscription.yaml.example (a 0.00 placeholder) is
# committed. The OTel export is local runtime data.
config/subscription.yaml
data/otel_export.jsonl

# Telemetry Layer B (ADR-0020): the dashboard is generated to the OS temp dir,
# never the repo tree. This defensive entry only matters if a future flag ever
# redirects the conventional filename into the working tree — it must not be
# committed (it carries personal cost/fee figures).
telemetry_dashboard.html

# Calibration loop runtime artifacts (ADR-0024) — per-run proposals + run log
memory/calibration-proposals/
metrics/calibration_log.jsonl

# Per-call token/cache log (SPEC-20260716-093231): grows per model call —
# durability is on-disk, not in git (committed Layer-2 artifacts stay the DB
# aggregates; see the ADR-0020 implementation note on the JSONL-vs-table call).
metrics/model_call_log.jsonl
